Implement user story SKY-004-B: Static dashboard HTML and build/start configuration

## Story Description
Create src/public/index.html as a styled single-page dashboard with search form and client-side JS. Wire GET / to serve it via fs.readFileSync at runtime. Configure package.json build script to copy static assets to dist/public/ and add start script. Add supertest devDependencies.

## Acceptance Criteria
- src/public/index.html exists as a styled dashboard with: (1) full-width solid-color header bar (e.g. #1a73e8) with bold white title 'Skyscanner Dashboard' and subtitle; (2) centered white card (max-width ~700px, rounded corners) with 2-column grid search form: From/To IATA inputs row 1, Date/Adults inputs row 2, each with label; (3) full-width colored 'Search Flights' button; (4) status area with red error banner, gray empty message, success count; (5) client-side JS submitting GET /search via fetch, disabling button during request, rendering results table in-page
- GET / returns HTTP 200 with Content-Type text/html and body equal to contents of src/public/index.html read at runtime via fs.readFileSync — hardcoded inline HTML is NOT acceptable; this route is never gated by RAPIDAPI_KEY
- package.json contains a 'start' script with value 'node dist/server.js'
- package.json 'build' script produces dist/server.js such that `npm run build && npm run start` starts the server and GET /health returns HTTP 200
- Build script copies src/public/ into dist/public/ — after `npm run build`, dist/public/index.html exists and GET / serves the real dashboard file (not 404 or hardcoded fallback)
- supertest and @types/supertest are listed in package.json devDependencies
- `npx tsc --noEmit` exits 0 with no type errors
- The file path used by the GET / handler resolves correctly under both `tsx src/server.ts` (dev) and `node dist/server.js` (built)





